actions:
Keep one implementation. Make world/imagination.py's Imagination (hook-based) the engine and turn LatentImaginationPlanner into a thin PlannerP adapter that builds the hooks from model components:
- reward_fn = R_psi(b_t, e_a, b_{t+1}, e_g, signals) (selfeval/intrinsic.py IntrinsicReward) plus lambda_s * delta P(success) from ProspectEvaluator;
- value_fn = LifetimeValue / value head;
- cont = world_model.continue_prob;
- penalty = epistemic disagreement over all queried outcomes plus the latent ensemble.
- Test: in observation_only ProbeEnv the planner's scores vary across candidates (std > 0) and do not use the env reward.

Implement world/voi.py: decision_voi(model, req, info_actions, n_y=8, next_candidates=k) ->
- for each info action a_i: sample y ~ p(y | Z, B, a_i) from the particle mixture;
- B' = update(clone(B), a_i, y);
- Q(B', a') for a fixed candidate set via a one-step imagined score (R_psi + gamma V);
- VOI_i = mean_y max_a' Q(B', a') - max_a' Q(B, a') - cost(a_i);
- use common random numbers across a_i.
Expose it as a planner candidate scorer and as an exploration signal.
- Test: on ProbeEnv with an informative signal VOI(run_test) > 0, and with informative=False VOI(run_test) is about 0 (|.| < 0.1 x win).
